s to  contend with a different kind of  conservation problem how many moose  would be  in the highlands here do you think the  last estimate was 2400 give or take so  from an enigma perspective a healthy  herd is dependent on a healthy ecosystem  so 2400 we think it's good because the  carrying capacity  of the ecosystem serves the population  better than having a hyper-abundant  population moose weren't always so  abundant a century ago the population  was wiped out another species from  alberta was introduced and with no  natural predators left it flourished so  today in the absence of wolves in  unemagi in nova scotia what's going to  keep the population in check is the  humans the human human interaction  [Music]  without hunting moose would overrun the  highlands and over feed on the saplings  that regenerate the boreal forest  traditionally the migma would head  inland to hunt this time of year a way  of life disrupted by colonialism i have  the right to do this  but more importantly have the  responsibility and the migma fought so  hard for those rights they fought  incredibly hard for those rights  and how many were in your hunting party  that's where the guardians come in  hannah martin is with the confederacy of  mainland migma  it's a really important time for us as  migma people to be on the land here in  unamagi and  harvesting this resource it's more than  just a harvest it's everything for us  when a moose is harvested the antlers  are measured samples are collected  details from the hunters are recorded  all vital information to track and  monitor the health of the population we  really treat the moose the salmon  everything with respect and with honor  down from the highlands and along the  sweeping coast of cape breton  our guides lead us to a sacred place  this place has uh much uh spiritual  significance we're surrounded by rock  the rocks are the grandfathers they're  the keepers of the stories talked along  these limestone cliffs is glooscop's 